+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 -->
+
+# Project Governance
+
+This document describes the governance model for **AffineScript**.
+
+---
+
+## Project Governance Model
+
+AffineScript follows a **Benevolent Dictator For Life (BDFL)** governance model.
+This model is well-suited for solo maintainers and small project teams where rapid,
+consistent decision-making is more valuable than formal consensus processes.
+
+The BDFL has final authority on all project decisions, including technical direction,
+release schedules, contributor access, and community standards.
+
+> **Transition clause:** When the core team exceeds three active maintainers, this
+> project should transition to a **consensus-based governance model** with documented
+> voting procedures. That transition should itself be recorded as an Architecture
+> Decision Record (ADR) in `docs/decisions/`.
+
+---
+
+## Decision Making
+
+### Day-to-day decisions
+
+- The BDFL makes final decisions on all matters.
+- Routine decisions (bug fixes, dependency updates, minor improvements) may be made
+  by any maintainer with commit access.
+- Maintainers are expected to use good judgement and seek input on non-trivial changes.
+
+### Proposing changes
+
+- Contributors can propose changes by opening issues or pull requests.
+- Significant changes (new features, breaking changes, architectural shifts) should
+  be discussed in an issue before implementation begins.
+- The BDFL will provide a clear accept/reject decision with reasoning.
+
+### Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)
+
+- Significant technical decisions are documented as ADRs in `docs/decisions/`.
+- ADR statuses: `proposed`, `accepted`, `deprecated`, `superseded`, `rejected`.
+- See `.machine_readable/6a2/META.a2ml` for the machine-readable ADR index.
+
+---
+
+## Roles
+
+### BDFL (Benevolent Dictator For Life)
+
+- The project creator and ultimate decision-maker.
+- Sets the project's technical direction and long-term vision.
+- Has final say on all matters, including maintainer appointments and removals.
+- Responsible for ensuring the project adheres to RSR standards.
+
+### Maintainer
+
+- Has commit access to the repository.
+- Reviews and merges pull requests.
+- Triages issues and manages releases.
+- Upholds code quality, security standards, and the Code of Conduct.
+- Listed in [MAINTAINERS.adoc](../MAINTAINERS.adoc).
+
+### Contributor
+
+- Anyone who submits pull requests, opens issues, or participates in discussions.
+- Does not have direct commit access.
+- All contributors must follow the [Code of Conduct](../CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
+
+---
+
+## Licensing
+
+AffineScript is a **multi-licence** project. The licence of a file is determined by
+what kind of material it is, not by where it sits in the tree:
+
+| Material | Licence | SPDX | Folder text |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Core technology — compiler, tooling, **editor/IDE integrations** | **MPL-2.0** | `MPL-2.0` | `LICENSES/LICENSE-MPL-2.0` |
+| Documentation and prose | **CC-BY-SA-4.0** | `CC-BY-SA-4.0` | `LICENSES/LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0` |
+| Game content (`proposals/idaptik/`, game-specific `examples/`) | **AGPL-3.0-or-later** | `AGPL-3.0-or-later` | `LICENSES/LICENSE-AGPL-3.0` |
+| Foundational technologies (Gossamer, Burble) | **PMPL-1.0 / MPL-2.0-derived** | `LicenseRef-PMPL-1.0` | `LICENSES/LICENSE-PMPL-1.0` |
+
+The repository root `LICENSE` declares the primary posture
+(`SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0` + `SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0`), so the
+repository's GitHub licence chip resolves to **MPL-2.0**. The full classification
+guide is [docs/governance/LICENSING-GUIDE.md](../docs/governance/LICENSING-GUIDE.md);
+the machine-readable invariants are in
+[.machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile](../.machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile).
+
+### affinescript-dom (DOM connector)
+
+`affinescript-dom/` is **Core Technology** (an editor/IDE integration). Its code is
+licensed **MPL-2.0** and its documentation **CC-BY-SA-4.0**. It is **not** AGPL game
+content. Any pull request that changes its licence headers away from this posture must
+be rejected. Every licence change to a connector, the `LICENSES/` folder, or the root
+`LICENSE` requires explicit BDFL review (enforced via `.github/CODEOWNERS`).
+
+---
+
+## Code of Conduct
+
+All participants are expected to follow the [Code of Conduct](../CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
+The BDFL serves as the final arbiter in conduct disputes.
+
+---
+
+## Amendments
+
+This governance document may be amended by the BDFL at any time. Amendments are
+documented as an ADR in `docs/decisions/` and committed with a clear message.
+
+---
